schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Common Crypto Scams and How to Spot Them
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    A plain-language field guide to the main crypto scam patterns —
    phishing, investment/"guaranteed returns" fraud, romance/"pig butchering"
    scams, and rug pulls — plus the psychological levers (urgency, authority,
    trust) scammers reuse, practical defenses (hardware wallets, 2FA,
    bookmarked URLs, multi-sig for shared funds), and what to do if you've
    been scammed (stop contact, document, report to IC3, alert your
    community).
  audience: community organisers and newcomers to Web3
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      article notes AI is now used to generate convincing scam content/voices,
      which erodes "professional appearance" as a trust signal
  related_concepts:
    - phishing
    - rug-pull
    - pig-butchering-scam
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/common-scams.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
